Built in JS (adding rows) — the plan says one encontro present by default; JS can add the row. I'll create the row markup in JS to avoid duplication. Use a <template>? Simpler: JS builds rows. Since JS builds rows, in HTML just have the container `<div id="lista-encontros"></div>` and the add button. On creation open, JS renders first row.

Note: labels for dynamically added rows need for/id for a11y. I'll generate unique ids `encontro-i-inicio`/`encontro-i-fim` with labels.

Confirm section: show after success. Place inside form, before submit button, hidden.

### app.js
Add element refs: botaoNovaAtividade, secaoCriacao, botaoCancelarCriacao, statusCriacao, formCriacao, campoTitulo, campoTipo, campoSala, campoVagas, listaEncontros, botaoAdicionarEncontro, confirmacaoCriacao.

Functions:
- `abrirCriacao()`: hide grade, show criacao, reset form (clear title, reset select tipo to palestra, clear sala options then load salas, clear vagas, clear lines then add one, hide confirmation, clear status).
